<title>FINLAND: MERITA TO LOWER PRIME RATE TO 3.75 PCT.</title>
<headline>MERITA TO LOWER PRIME RATE TO 3.75 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish bank group Merita Oy said in a statement on Tuesday it will lower its prime reference rate to 3.75 percent from 4.25 percent on December 1.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis for the cut are the continued decline in market interest rates, a prevailing favourable economic outlook and moderate inflation expectations,&quot; Merita said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
